Subject: marked: the transcript autolink's start search is bounded

What: markedTranscriptAutolink's start searches at most 1,024 characters (plus the longest link prefix) of the rest of the paragraph and otherwise cuts the text before a whitespace run, falling back to the full search when there is none; the test lexes long paragraphs against an unbounded start and expects identical tokens.
Why: marked calls start once per inline text step with the whole rest of the paragraph, so the unbounded search was quadratic: a 131 KB single-paragraph reply scanned 71 MB (55 ms in V8) and now scans about 1 MB (about 6 ms).

